## PREAMBLE

This software is made available under the Get Paid To Contribute License. We believe open development produces better software and that contributors deserve compensation for their work. This License reflects those values by formalizing the relationship between developers and maintainers. This Preamble is provided for informational purposes only and does not modify, expand, or limit the terms of this License.

## 1. DEFINITIONS

**"Software"**: The source code, documentation, and associated materials made available under this License.

**"Contribution"**: Any modification, addition, or improvement to the Software submitted to the Company through its designated contribution channels (e.g., pull requests to the official repository or other submission mechanisms specified in the Software's documentation).

**"Project"**: A proposed feature, enhancement, or body of work that has been submitted by a contributor or identified by the Company and approved in writing by the Company prior to commencement, with agreed-upon scope and compensation.

**"Standard Contribution"**: A Contribution submitted without prior approval, such as an unsolicited pull request. Standard Contributions are compensated according to the Standard Contribution Schedule set forth in Appendix A.

**"Commercial Use"**: Any use intended for or directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation, including use by or on behalf of a legal entity with revenue-generating activities. Commercial Use does not include internal evaluation, testing, or security review for a period not to exceed ninety (90) days, provided the Software is not deployed in production or used to provide services to third parties during such period.

**"Personal Use"**: Use by a natural person for private, non-commercial purposes that do not generate revenue, whether directly or indirectly. Use by or on behalf of any legal entity, regardless of size, does not qualify as Personal Use.

**"Extension"**: A distinct software module, plugin, extension, or integration that interfaces with the Software through its documented APIs, extension points, or public interfaces, and that does not incorporate substantial portions of the Software's core functionality.

**"Competing Product"**: Any product or service that replicates or substitutes for the core functionality of the Software, whether in whole or in part. Core functionality refers to the integrated workspace platform combining communication, documents, task management, and related productivity features as described in the Software's official documentation.

**"Acceptance"**: The merge of a Contribution into the Software's primary codebase by an authorized representative of the Company.

